%I A402745 #15 Nov 27 2026 16:55:01
%S A402745 31696783523,31696783549,31696783609,31696783637,31696783901,
%T A402745 31696784069,31696784107,31696784129,31696784137,31696784149,
%U A402745 31696784213,31696784233,31696784239,31696784267,31696784321,31696784351,31696785847,31696785877,31696785917,31696785949,31696785959
%N A402745 Primes p for which pi_{120;7,103,29,101}(p) - pi_{120;1,49,83,107}(p) = -1, where pi_{m;a,b,...}(x) is the number of primes <= x which are congruent to a or b or ... (mod m).
%C A402745 This sequence is about one of the 105 prime races modulo 120 between cosets of index 8 in (Z/120Z)* containing (Z/120Z)*^2; see A401958 for more details. Specifically, here we have H = {1,49,83,107} and S = {7,103,29,101}, corresponding to T = {chi_{-8}, chi_12, chi_{-15}, chi_40}, where chi_d = (d/.) is the Kronecker symbol viewed as a character modulo N = 120. Note that (Z/120Z)*^2 = {1,49}, and {83,107}, {7,103}, {29,101} are cosets of it in (Z/120Z)*.
%C A402745 Assuming GRH and LI, the set of x with pi_{120;7,103,29,101}(x) > pi_{120;1,49,83,107}(x) has logarithmic density 0.99890, making the race between {1,49,83,107} and {7,103,29,101} the 21st most biased among the 105 races between cosets of index 8 in (Z/120Z)*; see the Zenodo preprint "Logarithmic densities of prime number races between the cosets of subgroups containing the squares modulo 120" below.
%C A402745 Let D(x) = pi_{120;7,103,29,101}(x) - pi_{120;1,49,83,107}(x). (We have D(x0) = 50327 for x0 = 7*10^12; for the concrete numbers of primes below x0 in each congruence class modulo 120, see the file "pi_mod120_at_7e12.csv" in the Zenodo preprint). There is only one sign-changing zone giving a total of 18373 terms below x0:
%C A402745   a(1..18373) = 31696783523-31817999753 (there are 2752857 primes a(1) <= p <= a(18373) such that D(p) < 0, with D(p) reaching a minimum of -636 at p = 31733607803).
%H A402745 Jianing Song, <a href="/A402745/b402745.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..18373</a> (all terms below 7*10^12)
%H A402745 Leandro Hector Gallego, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24516487">Logarithmic densities of prime number races between the cosets of subgroups containing the squares modulo 120</a>, preprint, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A402745 Greg Martin and Daniel Fiorilli, <a href="https://personal.math.ubc.ca/~gerg/slides/Chennai-31Aug10.pdf">Prime number races: An asymptotic formula for the densities</a>, Analytic and Combinatorial Number Theory, Institute of Mathematical Sciences, Chennai, India. August 31, 2010.
%H A402745 Greg Martin, <a href="https://personal.math.ubc.ca/~gerg/slides/Canberra-29Nov18.pdf">Prime number races</a>, Pure Math Seminar, UNSW Canberra. November 29, 2018.
%H A402745 Andrey S. Shchebetov, <a href="https://math101.guru/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/01-A3-Presentation-v7.3EN-no.pdf">Testing Chebyshev's bias for prime numbers up to 10^15</a>, EUCYS 2018.
%H A402745 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chebyshev%27s_bias">Chebyshev's bias</a>.
%o A402745 (PARI) my(k=0, r=0); forprime(p=2, 1e11, r=p%120; if(r==1||r==49||r==83||r==107, k--); if(r==7||r==29||r==101||r==103, k++); if(k==-1, print1(p, ", ")))
%Y A402745 Cf. Races between cosets of index 8 in (Z/120Z)*: A298821 (11th), A297450 (19th), this sequence (21st), A295356 (23rd), A402746 (25th).
%Y A402745 See A401958 for races between cosets of index 4 in (Z/24Z)*.
%K A402745 nonn,new
%O A402745 1,1
%A A402745 _Leandro Hector Gallego_ and _Jianing Song_, Nov 26 2026
